      "crash": "beanpod/harness/0801_fuzz/df_fuzz/run:id:1376d84cebfb4ee656fc9380ae7088d4_136434892458543670419172517310157985751/out/default/crashes/id:000000,sig:06,src:000001,time:372,execs:43,op:havoc,rep:6",
      "note": "none of our test devices ships this TA, so it was not reproduced on device",
      "poc": "beanpod/pocs/0801_df_oob",
      "ta_name": "ifaa-key",
      "ta_path": "beanpod/tas/08010203000000000000000000000000.ta",
      "poc_note": "The shipped PoC does not reproduce this vulnerability in the emulator, and not because of race timing: it modifies cs->buffer[0x1000/4-2], i.e. roughly offset 0xffc of the shared buffer, while every double fetch Exploration recorded for this TA is in its first 32 bytes (offsets 0x17, 0x1b and 0x1f - the crash pinned here is a 1-byte second fetch at 0x1b, which Fetch-Anchored Fuzzing crashes with 0xc0). The PoC therefore never writes the byte that is double-fetched. Most likely it targets the Kinibi build of the TA (Table II lists it as Kinibi,Beanpod) or a different command than the harness uses; the emulated binary is the Beanpod one. Until that is resolved, reproduce this entry with 'e5_vulns --replay', which also gets the Distillation verdict that the crash needs the shared-memory race."
    },
